osed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-05-19T23:43:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T19:30:26Z","closed_at":"2025-05-20T16:39:44Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106614","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106614","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106614.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106614.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-20T16:39:44Z"},"body":"Closes #106379\r\n\r\nOpenGL was not using a swap-chain tied to a display or a CALayer that manages vsync, so it was running at an unbounded frame rate and causing stutter. This PR introduces changes to track the CG display for the window displaying the embedded content, and passes the CG display ID to the embedded process, so that a `CVDisplayLink` can be associated with the correct display. As the window moves from displays, it adjusts its frame rate accordingly. My system, with 120 Hz and 60 Hz displays, the frame rate changes correctly as I move the window on each screen.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_eve